Subject: [PATCH 00403/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for HARDEN the banked
 verifier product: characterize its GAMING-RESISTANCE. Take cached FoVer step
 triples and apply PROGRAMMATIC gaming perturbations
 (plausible-looking-but-wrong arithmetic, operand swaps, sign flips, padded
 reasoning that does not change the wrong answer) to the candidate steps, then
 measure whether the shipped 4-verifier ensemble still flags them (does the
 energy step-error signal degrade gracefully under adversarial-but-cheap
 perturbation?). CPU, cached -- NO live LLM, NO GPU candidate generation, NOT
 a moat/independence sweep. Product-robustness data for the deployable
 verifier; ties to arXiv:2604.15149. Reports a degradation curve, makes NO new
 headline claim.

